---
title: Jambalaya
course: main
cuisine: cajun
servings: 4
time_active: 25
time_total: 65
leftovers: great
tags: [one-pot, freezer-friendly]
---

Heat @olive oil{1%tbsp} in a #dutch oven{} over medium heat. Add @yellow onion{1}(diced), @green bell pepper{1}(diced), and @celery{2%stalks}(diced). Cook, stirring occasionally, until softened, ~{5-7%minutes}. Add @garlic{2%cloves}(minced) and cook ~{1%minute}.

Add @andouille sausage{1/2%lb}(sliced, or any smoked sausage) and @chicken breast{1/2%lb}(boneless, in bite-sized pieces). Cook until the chicken is no longer pink outside, ~{5%minutes}.

Stir in @smoked paprika{1%tsp}, @cajun seasoning{1%tsp}, @dried thyme{1/2%tsp}, and @?cayenne pepper{1/4%tsp}. Add @long-grain white rice{1%cup} and stir to coat in the spices, ~{1%minute}.

Add @diced tomatoes{1%can}(14.5 oz, drained), @chicken broth{1%cup}, @beef broth{1%cup}, and @bay leaves{2}. Bring to a boil, then cover and simmer on low until the rice is tender, ~{25-30%minutes}. Stir now and then, and add a splash of broth if it dries out.

Remove the bay leaves and season with @salt and @black pepper{}. Garnish with @green onions{2}(sliced) and @?fresh parsley{}(chopped).

> Keeps 3 days in the fridge or 2 months frozen. Kielbasa works in place of andouille.
